  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $f$ and $g$ be two real-valued continuous functions defined on the closed interval $[a,b]$, such that $f(a)<g(a)$ and $f(b)>g(b)$. Then the area enclosed between the graphs of the two functions and the lines $x=a$ and $x=b$ is always given by",
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\int_a^b|f(x)-g(x)|\\,dx$",
    "B": "$\\left|\\int_a^b(f(x)-g(x))\\,dx\\right|$",
    "C": "$\\left|\\int_a^b(|f(x)|-|g(x)|)\\,dx\\right|$",
    "D": "$\\int_a^b||f(x)|-|g(x)||\\,dx$."
  },
